  <rules><rule id="rule-20233" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, place a Grudge token next to it: up to 3 markers per enemy unit.

Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many tokens the target enemy unit has:
1- LoV units gain Stubborn when engaged with an enemy unit with a token.
2- LoV units gain Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens.
3- LoV units gain Preferred Enemy against an enemy unit with 3 tokens.

In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20234" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20235" name="Independent Character" hidden="false"><description>This model is an Independent Character.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20236" name="Grim Efficiency" hidden="false"><description>After deploying but before rolling to seize the initiative, as long as you have a model with this rule in your army, place a single Grudge Token on an enemy unit.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20237" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A model/unit entirely composed of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to "Run" in the shooting phase, always move 3".</description></rule><rule id="rule-20238" name="Eternal Warrior" hidden="false"><description>This model has the Eternal Warrior special rule.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20239" name="Destined" hidden="false"><description>Úthar can reroll either a single die to hit, to wound or a save roll once per turn.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20240" name="Warlord Trait: Ancestral Bearing" hidden="false"><description>The Warlord gains the Resolute special rule, and friendly units within 12" of the Warlord also benefit from the Resolute special rule. In addition, when determining assault results for any of your units in combat, add 1 to your total if your Warlord is locked in combat.</description></rule></rules>
  <infoLinks>
    </infoLinks>
