      <rules><rule id="rule-20251" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, place a Grudge token next to it: up to 3 markers per enemy unit.

Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many tokens the target enemy unit has:
1- LoV units gain Stubborn when engaged with an enemy unit with a token.
2- LoV units gain Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens.
3- LoV units gain Preferred Enemy against an enemy unit with 3 tokens.

In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20252" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A model/unit entirely composed of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to "Run" in the shooting phase, always move 3".</description></rule><rule id="rule-20253" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20254" name="Mounted Assault" hidden="false"><description>When deploying a unit with this rule that has purchased Sagitaur ATVs as dedicated transports, you may split the squad into separate units. Split the squad so that each Sagitaur ATV has its transport capacity as filled as possible. Each Sagitaur ATV and the models embarked within them is then considered separate units for all intents and purposes. Any remaining models that cannot embark upon the Sagitaur ATVs remain as their own unit.</description></rule></rules>
      <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="12" /></costs>
