                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Melee, Master Crafted, Rending, Votann Diplomacy (Rending attacks from this weapon ignore invulnerable saves)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile></profiles>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="5" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20127" name="Flâyre" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <profiles><profile id="prof-20128" name="Flâyre" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">+1</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Melee, Rending, Solar Radiance (Enemy units in contact with the bearer must take a blind test at the start of the assault phase)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile></profiles>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="15" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20129" name="Wayfarer's Grace" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <rules><rule id="rule-20130" name="Wayfarer's Grace" hidden="false"><description>The bearer gains the Feel No Pain (4+) special rule.</description></rule></rules>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="20" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20131" name="The Grey Crest" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <rules><rule id="rule-20132" name="The Grey Crest" hidden="false"><description>The bearer counts as having Defensive Grenades. Attacks against the bearer must reroll all to hit and to wound rolls of a '6'.</description></rule></rules>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="25" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20133" name="Grudge's End" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <profiles><profile id="prof-20134" name="Grudge's End" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">24"</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Assault 2, Enmity Protocols (Add 1 to the number of shots and strength of this weapon for each Grudge token on the target enemy unit)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile></profiles>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="15" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20135" name="Wârpestryk" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <rules><rule id="rule-20136" name="Wârpestryk" hidden="false"><description>Once per game during your movement phase if the bearer and their unit is unengaged, you may pick up and redeploy the bearer's unit anywhere exactly as if coming in from Deep Strike. Roll to scatter as normal.</description></rule></rules>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="20" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20137" name="The Hearthfist" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <profiles><profile id="prof-20138" name="The Hearthfist" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">+3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Melee, Unwieldy, Gets Hot, Searing Grasp (For each wound the bearer causes, inflict D3 automatic S4 AP- hits to the enemy unit)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile></profiles>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="25" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20139" name="The Murmuring Stave" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <rules><rule id="rule-20140" name="The Murmuring Stave" hidden="false"><description>Grimnyr only. The bearer generates an additional warp charge in the psychic phase. When manifesting a power against a unit with a Grudge token, add 1 to the psychic test roll.</description></rule></rules>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="20" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20141" name="Thyrikite Plate" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <rules><rule id="rule-20142" name="Thyrikite Plate" hidden="false"><description>The bearer changes their save to a 2+ and becomes immune to the Fleshbane and Poison special rules. If the attack has no strength value, it wounds on a roll of a '6'.</description></rule></rules>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="20" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20143" name="Vôlumm's Master Artifice" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <profiles><profile id="prof-20144" name="Vôlumm's Master Artifice" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">18"</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Heavy 1, Master Crafted, Graviton, Concussive, Beamer</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile></profiles>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="20" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="rl-20145" name="Ymmâ's Shield" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false">
          <rules><rule id="rule-20146" name="Ymmâ's Shield" hidden="false"><description>Einhyr Champion only. Attacks against the bearer suffer -1 Strength.</description></rule></rules>
          <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="15" /></costs>
        </selectionEntry></selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup></sharedSelectionEntryGroups><sharedRules><rule id="rule-20001" name="Assistant" hidden="false"><description>A model with this rule does not prevent their attached character from joining another unit, this unit simply joins the same unit as well.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20003" name="Brôkhyr's Guild" hidden="false"><description>In your shooting phase, instead of firing weapons, a character with this rule can repair a vehicle either in base contact or that they are embarked upon. To repair, roll a D6 and add +1 for each E-Cog in the unit. On a 5+, either restore a hull point or remove a Weapon Destroyed or Immobilised result from that vehicle. If this unit contains an Ironkin Assistant, you can pick two different effects on a successful repair roll, but not 2 of the same.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20004" name="Companion" hidden="false"><description>Models with this rule are treated as markers and are not targetable in any way. Models with this rule do not block line of sight and other models may move over and through models with this rule. When the attached character and their unit moves, place these models as close as possible to the attached character. When the attached character is slain, remove these models with this rule. Models with this rule may make attacks in the shooting/combat phase, in which case they can target any eligible models that their attached character can target. Models with this rule never gain the benefits for assaulting.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20005" name="Cyberstimms" hidden="false"><description>When slain in combat, a model with this rule is not removed as a casualty until after it makes its attacks this combat phase. If the model has already attacked when it was slain, then this rule does not take effect.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20006" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, place a Grudge token next to it: up to 3 markers per enemy unit.

Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many tokens the target enemy unit has:
1- LoV units gain Stubborn when engaged with an enemy unit with a token.
2- LoV units gain Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens.
3- LoV units gain Preferred Enemy against an enemy unit with 3 tokens.

In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20007" name="Grim Efficiency" hidden="false"><description>After deploying but before rolling to seize the initiative, as long as you have a model with this rule in your army, place a single Grudge Token on an enemy unit.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20008" name="Mounted Assault" hidden="false"><description>When deploying a unit with this rule that has purchased Sagitaur ATVs as dedicated transports, you may split the squad into separate units. Split the squad so that each Sagitaur ATV has its transport capacity as filled as possible. Each Sagitaur ATV and the models embarked within them is then considered separate units for all intents and purposes. Any remaining models that cannot embark upon the Sagitaur ATVs remain as their own unit.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20009" name="Resolute" hidden="false"><description>Units with this rule roll 3D6 when taking leadership tests, discarding the highest die.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20010" name="Spark of the Votann" hidden="false"><description>See "Power of the Machine Spirit" in the main rulebook.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20011" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A model/unit entirely composed of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to "Run" in the shooting phase, always move 3".</description></rule><rule id="rule-20012" name="Swivel Actuators" hidden="false"><description>Sponson weapons on a vehicle with this rule have a 180 field of fire rather than the usual 90 degrees.</description></rule><rule id="rule-20013" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule><rule id="usr-loneop-001" name="Lone Operative" hidden="false"><description>Unless this model has joined a unit, it can only be selected as the target of a ranged attack if the firing model is within 12".</description></rule></sharedRules></catalogue>